    "River Rea"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "I12",
   "kind": "point",
   "text": "Largest and most populous British city outside London.",
   "page": 1,
   "section": "notes",
   "topic": "BIRMINGHAM – West Midlands, England",
   "context": "",
   "marker": "",
   "bullet": true,
   "bold": [
    "Largest and most populous"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "I13",
   "kind": "point",
   "text": "Was a medium-sized market town in the medieval period; grew to international prominence in the 18th century.",
   "page": 1,
   "section": "notes",
   "topic": "BIRMINGHAM – West Midlands, England",
   "context": "",
   "marker": "",
   "bullet": true,
   "bold": [
    "18th century"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "I14",
   "kind": "point",
   "text": "At the heart of the Industrial Revolution – advances in science, technology & economic development.",
   "page": 1,
   "section": "notes",
   "topic": "BIRMINGHAM – West Midlands, England",
   "context": "",
   "marker": "",
   "bullet": true,
   "bold": [
    "Industrial Revolution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "I15",
   "kind": "point",
   "text": "The industrial steam engine (one of the most important inventions in British history) was invented here.",
   "page": 1,
   "section": "notes",
   "topic": "BIRMINGHAM – West Midlands, England",
   "context": "",
   "marker": "",
   "bullet": true,
   "bold": [
    "industrial steam engine"
   ]
  },
  {
