   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "I112",
   "kind": "answer",
   "text": "Explain why Edinburgh is an important financial centre. Edinburgh is the second largest financial centre in the UK after London. It has been a centre of banking for over 300 years. The Bank of Scotland was founded there in 1695 and the Royal Bank of Scotland (RBS) has its global headquarters in Edinburgh.",
   "page": 5,
   "section": "answers",
   "topic": "",
   "context": "",
   "marker": "4.",
   "bullet": false,
   "bold": [
    "Explain why Edinburgh is an important financial centre"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "I113",
   "kind": "answer",
   "text": "How did Cardiff rise from a small town to become the capital of Wales? Cardiff was a small town until the early 19th century. It became a major port for coal transport and grew into the world’s most important coal port. It was made a city in 1905 and was proclaimed the capital of Wales in 1955.",
   "page": 5,
   "section": "answers",
   "topic": "",
   "context": "",
   "marker": "5.",
   "bullet": false,
   "bold": [
